.TH "LMM" "1" "Nov 2026" "lmm 2.3.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-mod-fomod - Change an installed mod's FOMOD installer choices


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm mod fomod <mod-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run an installed mod's FOMOD installer again, with the choices you made
last time preselected, and install what the new choices select.

.PP
The mod keeps its version: lmm fetches the same file again (or reuses one
it kept), asks the installer's questions one step at a time, and replaces
the deployed files with the new selection. The new choices are recorded on
the profile.

.PP
A mod installed before lmm ran FOMOD installers went in as the whole
archive; this runs its installer and replaces that install.

.PP
Without a terminal, answer with --fomod-choices <file.json> or
--fomod-defaults; with neither, the questions are printed (the full
document under --json) and lmm exits non-zero.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm mod fomod 12604 --game skyrim-se
  lmm mod fomod 12604 --game skyrim-se --fomod-choices choices.json


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--fomod-choices\fP=""
	answer FOMOD installer questions from a JSON file (the profile's fomod: shape or Vortex's choices array; key it by source:id when several mods ask)

.PP
\fB--fomod-defaults\fP[=false]
	answer FOMOD installer questions with the installer's own preselection

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--force\fP[=false]
	overwrite other mods' files without asking, and continue past failing hooks

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fomod

.PP
\fB--skip-verify\fP[=false]
	skip checksum verification of the download


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--source\fP=""
	mod source; "local" names an imported mod (default: the source the installed mod carries, else the game's sole configured source; prompts when several are configured)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


